    "body": "Hmm… True. Now, reflecting on this I see that `prev_bg` was transitive because we go through the sequences in order so any reference to the previous style is known because we keep a reference to the previous style. Were I to do the same for forward colour references, I would have to first go through the sequences in reverse order, resolve the forward references and then process the sequences like it is currently done. But TBH, I don't really know how to to this in Rust. should I just generate a new `segments` where I would `segment.copy()` with partially resolved styles?",
