    "body": "Ah I see that I can use `Peekable::nth` to look further that the next element so I can do transitive. However it feels suboptimal. Worst case scenario is all the segments are references to the very last then I traverse the vector *n×(n+1)/2*. It should be fine since I expect the segments vector size to be less than 10 and the number of references to be no more than 1 or 2 segments away. But still. It bothers me a bit. ",
